{%- comment -%}
  House of Agha · Qutb Shahi pattern (2026-10-06). The one architectural ornament of the site,
  replacing the old diamond jaali (assets/hoa-jaali.svg). Drawn from Qutb Shahi arches and
  their stucco: a pointed, shouldered arch, a thin inner arch, a carved lotus in the spandrel,
  and Hyderabad's monuments. Geometry lives only in the assets below; this snippet is the markup side, and CSS that
  needs the motif inside a pseudo-element masks the same files.

    frieze    assets/hoa-qutb.svg        an arcade band that repeats seamlessly (48×24 tile)
    arch      assets/hoa-qutb-arch.svg   one arch with a lotus inside, a single mark
    ornament  assets/hoa-qutb-lotus.svg  the lotus boss alone, a small mark
    heritage  assets/hoa-qutb-heritage.svg  Hyderabad's monuments in line (Charminar, a Qutb Shahi
              tomb, Golconda Fort, Mecca Masjid) with lotuses between, standing on the arcade
              frieze at half size: the heritage pattern and the monuments in one band (240×52
              tile, seamless; regenerate with tools/gen-qutb-heritage.py)
    textile   assets/hoa-qutb-textile.svg  Deccani textile ground: Himroo-style keri (paisley)
              butis in a half-drop with four-dot phool seeds (40×40 tile, both axes)
    bidri     assets/hoa-qutb-bidri.svg    Bidri inlay border: a scrolling vine, four-petal flowers
              and leaves between double rules; meant in silver on a dark ground (80×20 tile)
    floral    assets/hoa-qutb-floral.svg   Hyderabadi floral: the eight-petal stucco rosette in a
              double roundel, as in Qutb Shahi spandrels (a single mark)

  Colour is currentColor (set `color` on the element or its parent); size with --qutb-h on a
  frieze (keep it even so the tile width stays a whole pixel), width/height on the others.
  Styles: assets/hoa-home.css, "QUTB SHAHI PATTERN".

  Params: variant ('frieze' | 'arch' | 'ornament' | 'heritage' | 'textile' | 'bidri' | 'floral', default 'frieze'), class, attrs (raw
  attributes, e.g. 'data-hoa-ab-orn'). Decorative only, always aria-hidden.

  {% render 'hoa-qutb-pattern', variant: 'frieze', class: 'hoa-footer__frieze' %}
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign qutb_variant = variant | default: 'frieze'
  assign qutb_known = 'frieze,arch,ornament,heritage,textile,bidri,floral' | split: ','
  unless qutb_known contains qutb_variant
    assign qutb_variant = 'frieze'
  endunless
-%}
<span class="hoa-qutb hoa-qutb--{{ qutb_variant }}{% if class != blank %} {{ class }}{% endif %}" aria-hidden="true"{% if attrs != blank %} {{ attrs }}{% endif %}></span>
